:: OC Erin Lunchroom Bullying [nobr]

/* Written by: Zexion */
/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 15>>
The lunchroom is a cacophony of shouting students and the rhythmic clatter of plastic trays. You’ve just managed to secure a spot at a relatively quiet table near one of the entrances and start eating when you spot a familiar shock of black hair a few rows over. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> is sitting alone, his shoulders hunched as he stares intently at a delicious-looking slice of pizza, trying his best to not look like he’s too excited for the food.<br>
<br>
The peaceful moment doesn't last. <span style="color:yellow">A shadow falls over <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span>’s table as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> and two of his usual goons swagger over. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> doesn't even say a word at first; he just reaches down and drags <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span>’s tray toward himself with a screech of plastic against wood.</span> <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "OC Erin",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
            Mouth: "Frown",
            Eyes: "Mad",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "Michael",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
            Mouth: "Smirk",
            Eyes: "Mad",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">"Hey, thanks for the snack, emo-kid,"</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> sneers, picking up the pizza slice. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">"You look like you’re on a diet anyway. Too much brooding makes you lose your appetite, right?"</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> stiffens, his hands clenching into fists on the tabletop. He looks up, his eyes flashing with a brief spark of anger before he forces himself to lean back, trying to maintain that "unbothered" persona. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">"Real original, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>. What’s next? You going to pull my hair? Just take it and go. You clearly need the calories more than I do."</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>’s grin turns sharp. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">"I think I’ll take the drink, too."</span> He grabs the milk carton, <span style="color:yellow">purposely tipping it over so a splash of white liquid puddles across the table, narrowly missing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span>’s hoodie.</span> Laughing, the group saunters off to their own table, taking the tray with the rest of the food, <span style="color:yellow">leaving <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> sitting in front of an empty, wet space.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> stares at the puddle for a long moment. He doesn't look around to see who's watching, but you can see the tips of his ears turning a bright, humiliated red. <span style="color:yellow">He reaches into his pockets, likely trying to act like the lunch-snatching didn't bother him, but his expression falls— probably crestfallen that his food was stolen.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:yellow">You look down at your own tray, which is still full with only a single bite taken, and then back at the boy sitting alone across the aisle.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Share your lunch with Erin<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You stand up, picking up your tray, and navigate through the crowded tables until you’re standing directly across from him. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> doesn't look up at first, his gaze fixed on the floor. You slide your tray onto the table, nudging his arm with the edge of it to get his attention. <br>
        
        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Smile",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "OC Erin",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I don’t need your pity, new kid,”</span> he mutters, though his eyes dart toward your food. You realize a problem: other than the milk, all the food on your tray requires a fork to eat. Since there’s only one fork—<span style="color:pink">the one already in your mouth</span>—you realize the implications. Pulling the plastic utensil out of your mouth, you jokingly tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> that he has two choices: <span style="color:yellow">he can either feed himself using your used fork, or you can feed him like a little baby.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Go fuck yourself with that fag shit!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> snaps, his face turning a deeper shade of red. He tells you to get lost, and for a while, you both sit in a tense, awkward silence. However, as the minutes tick by and the smell of the food becomes too much, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span>’s resolve finally breaks. He looks at you with a desperate, defeated expression. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Fine… will you still share?”</span> <br>
        <br>
        You grin, demanding that if he wants the food, you’re going to feed him like a baby—<span style="color:pink">though you promise not to make any embarrassing airplane noises.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> looks like he wants to disappear into the floor, but he’s too hungry to refuse. He leans forward, closing his eyes in shame as you hand-feed him the remainder of your lunch. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:pink">Despite his angry exterior, there’s something almost cute about how much his “tough guy” act has crumbled just for a few bites of cafeteria food.</span> <br>
        <<socialChange "Erin" 1 1>>
        <br>
        <<include "School Lunch">>
        <<set $FriendLunch to 1>>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Leave him alone<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You watch the scene unfold from a distance. As <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> sits there in front of the spilled milk, you find yourself hesitant to get involved. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> is still in a foul mood, and drawing attention to yourself might just make things worse for both of you. You look down at your tray and continue eating in silence while occasionally stealing glances. <br>
        <br>
        After a few minutes, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> realizes he’s becoming a spectacle for the nearby tables. He stands up abruptly, ignoring the mess on the table. He doesn't look at anyone as he stalks out of the lunchroom, his hands shoved deep into his pockets, and his head bowed. <br>
        
        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "OC Erin",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Eyes: "Sad",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Cry: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

        You, however, catch a glimpse of his face as he passes by, <span style="color:lightcoral">his lips wobbling and tears beginning to form in his eyes as he tries not to cry. If that wasn’t enough humiliation, the boy's stomach growls, causing him to pick up speed, sprinting the last few feet out of the room. Frowning, you wonder if you should feel bad for not helping him. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Erin</span> may act like a bad boy, but with his size and his tendency to just run his mouth, he’s as harmless as an emo-flavored <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>.</span> You decide maybe you’ll help him next time, as long as he doesn’t intentionally antagonize you or anyone else who might actually knock his teeth out. <br>
        <br>
        <<include "School Lunch">>
        <<set $FriendLunch to 1>>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>